&lt;p&gt;Spectral reflectance upsampling, or reflectance recovery, is the process of converting tristimulus values into spectral reflectance distributions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This document explores the Gaussian-based spectral upsampling method implemented in &lt;a href="https://github.com/colour-science/colour"&gt;Colour&lt;/a&gt; on the &lt;code&gt;develop&lt;/code&gt; branch as of this writing. The method uses clamped Gaussian basis spectra with the hierarchical decomposition algorithm from &lt;em&gt;Smits (1999)&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.colour-science.org/posts/gaussian-based-spectral-upsampling/"&gt;Read more…&lt;/a&gt; (9 min remaining to read)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description><category>colorchecker classic</category><category>colour</category><category>colour science</category><category>reflectance</category><category>RGB colourspace</category><category>spectral</category><guid>https://www.colour-science.org/posts/gaussian-based-spectral-upsampling/</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Jan 2026 08:00:00 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>Colour Checker Detection with Machine Learning</title><link>https://www.colour-science.org/posts/colour-checker-detection-with-machine-learning/</link><dc:creator>Colour Developers</dc:creator><description>&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;We have released a new version of &lt;a class="reference external" href="https://github.com/colour-science/colour-checker-detection/releases/tag/v0.2.0"&gt;Colour - Checker Detection&lt;/a&gt;
that implements a new machine learning inference method to detect colour
rendition charts, specifically the &lt;em&gt;ColorChecker Classic 24&lt;/em&gt; from
&lt;em&gt;X-Rite&lt;/em&gt; / &lt;em&gt;Calibrite&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This post describes the journey to produce the model and package it with
&lt;strong&gt;Colour - Checker Detection&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.colour-science.org/posts/colour-checker-detection-with-machine-learning/"&gt;Read more…&lt;/a&gt; (10 min remaining to read)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description><category>colorchecker classic</category><category>colour</category><category>colour science</category><category>cvat</category><category>hugging face</category><category>inference</category><category>machine learning</category><category>roboflow</category><category>yolo</category><guid>https://www.colour-science.org/posts/colour-checker-detection-with-machine-learning/</guid><pubDate>Thu, 11 Jan 2024 04:48:50 GMT</pubDate></item></channel></rss>